  "statement": "A fraction a/b is called in its lowest form if gcd(a, b) = 1. It is possible to express a/b using the sum of a finite number of reciprocals of natural numbers. For example, 2/7 can be written as 1/4 + 1/28. Such a representation is called an Egyptian fraction representation of a/b.",
